From 25b9110d724add867937c8a87e60d0b0898e4bf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:05:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 103/109] media: sc7730: S5K4ECGX stills up to 2576x1932 and
 autofocus

The S5K4ECGX has its own ISP with a separate capture configuration and
an autofocus engine; the stock HAL drives both through I2C writes to the
firmware's interface words. Do the same in the sensor driver:

- Still modes 1600x1200, 2048x1536, 2560x1920 and 2576x1932 behind the
  parameter s5k4ecgx.still_modes (default off, so clients that pick the
  largest size keep the preview sizes). As the HAL does, the sensor
  starts a 640x480 preview, lets AE settle (still_settle_ms), runs one
  autofocus search (still_af), writes the capture size table and
  switches with EnableCapture / NewConfigSync / EnableCaptureChanged,
  all before the receiver starts; the DCAM drops still_skip frames.
- Autofocus controls on the subdev: V4L2_CID_AUTO_FOCUS_RANGE (normal /
  macro lens tables as firmware files), _START (one search: AfCmd 5, then
  the coarse status at 0x70002eee and the fine status at 0x70002207),
  _STOP and _STATUS; preview_af_ms runs one search after a preview start.
- The AF actuator supply (afvdd) is SC2723 vddcammot, 2.8 V.

DCAM: frames wider than the 2048 pixel line buffer of path 1 go through
path 2 (4096). The path registers, interrupts, copy and reset bits come
from a table now; NV12 uses the scaler at 1:1 on either path (its
coefficient RAM sits at 0x400 for path 1 and 0x1400 for path 2, so the
register window grows to 0x2000). The pre-skip comes from the sensor.

Device tree: vddcammot as afvdd-supply, I2C0 at 400 kHz (both sensors
carry SENSOR_I2C_FREQ_400 in the stock HAL; the S5K init drops from 1.8
to about 0.5 s), CMA 128 MiB for 5 MP buffers.

Tested in the rescue system: preview unchanged (rear 16 fps, front 24
fps); autofocus reached after 1.4 s, Laplacian variance 245 -> 556;
1600x1200 and 2048x1536 through path 1, 2560x1920 and 2576x1932 through
path 2 at 7.7 fps in NV12 with correct colours, no writes past the
buffers.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
